<!-- Section 1: sec-intro -->
<section id="sec-intro" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Similar Right Triangles Calculator</h2>
  <p>Find scale factors and missing sides of similar right triangles.</p>
  <p>Two right triangles are similar when their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. They keep the same shape even when their sizes differ, because both contain a 90° angle and their acute angles match. The angles never change when a triangle is scaled; only the side lengths grow or shrink.</p>
  <p><span set:html={rich('[[[k=\\frac{18}{6}=3]]]')} /></p>
  <p>The Similar Right Triangles Calculator offers three modes. Find Scale Factor compares one pair of matching sides. Find Missing Similar Side multiplies an original side by <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} />. Find Original Side divides a similar side by <span set:html={rich('[[k]]')} />. Take an original side of <span set:html={rich('[[6]]')} /> and a matching similar side of <span set:html={rich('[[18]]')} />: the scale factor is <span set:html={rich('[[3]]')} />, so the similar triangle is three times as large in every linear dimension, while every angle stays exactly the same.</p>
</section>

<!-- Section 2: sec-calculate -->
<section id="sec-calculate" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
